Lei das Duplicatas (Lei 5.474/1968), Lei dos Cartórios (Lei 8.935/1994), Lei Orgânica do TCU (Lei 8.443/1992) and Lei dos Juizados Especiais Federais (Lei 10.259/2001) verified 2026-10-31: replay of each act's annotated Planalto page (26 versions) against Planalto's consolidated page (l5474compilado.htm) and, for the other three (no consolidated page), the unstruck text of their pages: 0 differences except the Lei 5.474 ementa set as a heading on the consolidated page (layout, explained); 0 problems. In-force days from the acts' own clauses (Lei 5.474 art. 28: 30 days; Lei 10.259 art. 27: six months, 14.1.2002; the others on publication). Hand facts from the official pages: Lei 5.474 arts. 15-18 as Decreto-Lei 436/1969 left them (its text keeps art. 15 §§ 1-11) end with Lei 6.458/1977's new Capítulo V; Lei 14.206/2021 in force on publication (28.9.2021); law:lei-14301-2022 repinned (the cited link pointed at Lei 5.474's page); Resolução do Senado Federal nº 16/2006 (DOU 15.3.2006) suspends an expression of Lei 8.443 art. 55 § 1º (split rule, kind law); Lei 8.443's mixed-case heading read for the start-of-act test. Vigência fallback audit clean; duplicate-label, duplicate-line, first-line and note-leak checks clean (only '(Revogado)' placeholders); parse twice identical (sha256 fcaf9391); merged scratch build 97 acts, 1936 versions, 1653 commits, check.py 0 mismatches, 0 trailer errors, --compare identical, audit_push clean on main and futuro.
